<h2 id="verifying-youbot" class="max-md:pr-4" data-state="closed" data-fern-style="cursor:pointer">Verifying YouBot</h2>
<p>Since user agent strings can be spoofed, You.com supports three ways to verify that requests are genuinely from YouBot: cryptographic signatures (recommended), reverse DNS checks, and IP range validation.</p>
<h3 id="cloudflare-web-bot-auth" class="max-md:pr-4" data-state="closed" data-fern-style="cursor:pointer">Cloudflare Web Bot Auth</h3>
<p>YouBot uses <strong class="font-semibold">Cloudflare’s Web Bot Auth</strong> standard for authentication. This cryptographic verification ensures that requests claiming to be from YouBot are legitimate.</p>
<p>To verify YouBot requests:</p>
<ol class="mb-3 list-outside list-decimal [&amp;_ol]:!list-[lower-roman]">
<li class=""><strong class="font-semibold">Check the HTTP Message Signatures</strong> in the request headers</li>
<li class=""><strong class="font-semibold">Retrieve the public keys</strong> from You.com’s well-known directory:<!-- -->
